        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data, and — because `execute = TRUE` — **actually ran it**. We examined 5 R code files.",
          "#### Run order",
          "The scripts were ordered by their data dependencies (a script writing a file another reads runs first), `source()` calls, and numeric filename prefixes.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1:5, File = c(\"json_dump.R\", \"missing_input.R\", \n\"parse_error.R\", \"writes_then_reads.R\", \"reads_written.R\"), \"Runs after\" = c(\"—\", \n\"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"writes_then_reads.R\"), Basis = c(\"none\", \n\"none\", \"none\", \"none\", \"dependency\")), row.names = c(NA, -5L\n), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "Every data path in the code works in the repository as deposited.",
          "#### Files the deposit does not hold",
          "The scripts that did not run through read 1 data file that is not in the deposit, and no script of the deposit writes: `not_in_repo.csv`.",
          "#### Parsing",
          "1 R file did not parse and cannot be run (see code_check for the errors).",
          "#### Non-R content detected",
          "1 file that failed to parse is not actually R content (a JSON/HTML/XML dump saved with an R-type extension) -- this is informational, not a reproducibility defect.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"json_dump.R\", Detected = \"not_r_content\", \n    Detail = \"file content does not appear to be R (detected: JSON)\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Execution",
          "**The code was run.** Each script ran in an isolated subprocess against a throwaway copy of the repository, in the run order above, with a 60-second per-script timeout. Of 4 scripts: 2 ran without error, 1 errored, 0 timed out, 0 could not run because one of its own dependencies is unavailable, 1 did not parse. Running against current package versions: a break can reflect version drift, which argues for pinning versions.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"json_dump.R\", \"missing_input.R\", \"parse_error.R\", \n\"writes_then_reads.R\", \"reads_written.R\"), Outcome = c(\"not_r_content\", \n\"errored\", \"not_parsed\", \"ran_ok\", \"ran_ok\"), Detail = c(\"\", \n\"runtime\", \"\", \"\", \"\"), \"Time (s)\" = 0), row.names = c(NA, \n-5L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "*Expand a row below to see the output each script produced.*",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — missing_input.R (errored)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> dat <- read.csv(\"not_in_repo.csv\")\n````\n**Messages / errors (stderr):**\n````\nError in file(file, \"rt\") : cannot open the connection\nIn addition: Warning message:\nIn file(file, \"rt\") :\n  cannot open file 'not_in_repo.csv': No such file or directory\n````\n\n:::\n",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — writes_then_reads.R (ran_ok)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> dat <- read.csv(\"data.csv\")\n> summ <- data.frame(mean_x = mean(dat$x))\n> write.csv(summ, \"intermediate.csv\", row.names = FALSE)\n````\n\n:::\n",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — reads_written.R (ran_ok)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> summ <- read.csv(\"intermediate.csv\")\n> print(summ$mean_x)\n[1] 4\n````\n\n:::\n"
